{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1553011068,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjI4MTUwNzc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3248","origin":"github"},"title":"rev-save -r doesn't save full dataset hierarchy","message":"I'm working on switching `run` over to using `rev_save` and bringing in -revolution's run tests.  In the process, I was replacing a `.add(\".\", recursive=True)` call in `test_run_inputs_outputs` with `.rev_save(recursive=True)` and couldn't get `rev_save` to save the entire dataset hierarchy.\n\nI've isolated the setup from that test to the script at the bottom of this post.  Here's an overview of the differences:\n\n```\n% datalad status -d saved-with-add -r\n% datalad status -d saved-with-rev_save -r\n modified: s0 (dataset)\nuntracked: s0/s1_0 (directory)\nuntracked: s0/s1_1 (directory)\nuntracked: s0/ss (directory)\n\n% datalad subdatasets -d saved-with-add -r\nsubdataset(ok): s0 (dataset)\nsubdataset(ok): s0/s1_0 (dataset)\nsubdataset(ok): s0/s1_0/s2 (dataset)\nsubdataset(ok): s0/s1_1 (dataset)\nsubdataset(ok): s0/s1_1/s2 (dataset)\nsubdataset(ok): s0/ss (dataset)\naction summary:\n  subdataset (ok: 6)\n% datalad subdatasets -d saved-with-rev_save -r\nsubdataset(ok): s0 (dataset)\n```\n\nSo, `rev-save` adds s0 to the root dataset (save-with-rev_save) but doesn't seem to register the subdatasets further down the tree.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003escript\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\nimport os.path as op\nimport tempfile\n\nfrom datalad.api import Dataset\nfrom datalad.tests.utils import create_tree\n\ntempdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n\n\ndef add(ds):\n    ds.add(\".\", recursive=True)\n\n\ndef rev_save(ds):\n    ds.rev_save(recursive=True)\n\n\nfor savefn in [add, rev_save]:\n    root = op.join(tempdir, \"saved-with-\" + savefn.__name__)\n    create_tree(root,\n                {\"s0\": {\"s1_0\": {\"s2\": {\"a.dat\": \"a\",\n                                        \"b.txt\": \"b\"}},\n                        \"s1_1\": {\"s2\": {\"c.dat\": \"c\",\n                                        \"d.txt\": \"d\"}},\n                        \"ss\": {\"e.dat\": \"e\"}}})\n\n    for subds in [(\"s0\", \"s1_0\", \"s2\"),\n                  (\"s0\", \"s1_1\", \"s2\"),\n                  (\"s0\", \"s1_0\"),\n                  (\"s0\", \"s1_1\"),\n                  (\"s0\", \"ss\"),\n                  (\"s0\",)]:\n        Dataset(op.join(*((root,) + subds))).rev_create(force=True)\n    ds = Dataset(root).rev_create(force=True)\n    savefn(ds)\n\nprint(tempdir)\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null}]}